\subsection{The Task of Summarisation}
Summarisation in NLP is defined as the process of generating a concise and fluent representation of the input text \cite{mani2019survey}. The main goal of summarisation systems is to generate the summary with fluent and accurate content and preserve the essence of the input text. 
There are two main summarisation categories: abstractive summarisation and extractive summarisation. An extractive summarisation aims to generate a summary by extracting the most important sentences from the input text.

\paragraph{Sample Input}
\texttt{nazi}

\paragraph{Sample Output}
\texttt{fascist, racist}

